WEBVTT


00:00:25.044 --> 00:00:28.104
<i>Hold on 'cause I'm letting go</i>


00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.716
<i>I'm gonna lasso your heart like a rodeo</i>


00:00:31.884 --> 00:00:35.547
<i>I'm gonna give you some
Till you want some more</i>


00:00:35.721 --> 00:00:39.452
<i>'Cause all I see is an open door</i>


00:00:39.625 --> 00:00:43.425
<i>And I see where it's leading me
All of this energy</i>


00:00:43.595 --> 00:00:47.190
<i>Been bottled up way too long
It's powerful, powerful</i>


00:00:47.366 --> 00:00:50.927
<i>You see what I'm getting at
I'm ready for all of that</i>


00:00:51.103 --> 00:00:54.630
<i>If I'm not a star, you're blind</i>


00:00:54.807 --> 00:00:58.174
<i>I've got rings on my fingers
And glitter in my hair</i>


00:00:58.344 --> 00:01:01.609
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:05.477
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:05.651 --> 00:01:09.678
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:09.855 --> 00:01:13.450
<i>I've got high heel stilettos
And I'm kicking in doors</i>


00:01:13.625 --> 00:01:16.753
<i>And kissing your ass
Ain't what my lipstick's for</i>


00:01:16.929 --> 00:01:20.695
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:20.866 --> 00:01:23.858
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:24.036 --> 00:01:27.528
Where's breakfast?
I want waffles, spaghetti!


00:01:27.706 --> 00:01:30.971
Spaghetti waffles! Whoo. Whoo!


00:01:31.143 --> 00:01:33.168
Victor. Victor.
Please wait in the house, please.


00:01:34.613 --> 00:01:37.446
My body is entering hunger shock.


00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:42.514
Oh, bad news.
The cat pooped in the den.


00:01:42.688 --> 00:01:45.987
Worse news, I used your blanket
to clean it up.


00:01:46.158 --> 00:01:48.092
- We don't have a cat.
- No kidding.


00:02:23.195 --> 00:02:26.756
Oh. L... Sorry.
I didn't think you'd be awake.


00:02:26.932 --> 00:02:28.092
You have an appointment...


00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:30.861
...with Guy Morgan,
I didn't think you'd wanna be late.


00:02:31.036 --> 00:02:33.971
Oh, look at you thinking. Cute.


00:02:34.139 --> 00:02:36.198
But I always have time for my portrait.


00:02:36.375 --> 00:02:37.899
Look alive. Paint.


00:02:38.343 --> 00:02:40.174
I'm feeling spiritually blocked.


00:02:40.345 --> 00:02:42.176
Draw me a sesame seed bath.


00:02:42.614 --> 00:02:43.740
Bath. Now.


00:02:44.716 --> 00:02:46.581
Now, make momma look more beautiful
and thinner.


00:02:47.953 --> 00:02:49.181
And make that water more quiet.


00:02:52.758 --> 00:02:54.851
- Bev, you awake?
- Of course I'm awake.


00:02:55.027 --> 00:02:57.621
If I waited for you, I'd never be on time.


00:02:57.796 --> 00:03:00.230
Lucky you never wait for me then.


00:03:13.712 --> 00:03:15.145
Victor, no.


00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:23.754
Uh, don't you want a glass?


00:03:23.922 --> 00:03:29.918
Hmm. Earthy. A tad fishy.
Lovely gravel finish.


00:03:30.395 --> 00:03:32.920
Did you let Victor put worms
in the blender again?


00:03:33.632 --> 00:03:35.327
Yes. I mean, no.


00:03:36.835 --> 00:03:38.427
I mean, it just happened.


00:03:38.971 --> 00:03:40.336
You know nothing can kill me.


00:03:41.507 --> 00:03:43.134
Nothing.


00:03:47.779 --> 00:03:50.646
Step on it, Katie.
I cannot be late for this meeting.


00:03:50.816 --> 00:03:52.181
Just run them over if you have to.


00:03:54.987 --> 00:03:58.013
Hello? No, the kids don't need a library.


00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:01.421
I am the dean, and the dean gets
what she wants, and I wanna remodel.


00:04:01.593 --> 00:04:05.051
You're just boring. I'm being honest.
I don't know what else to tell you.


00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:08.324
And I wanted my office done
for my meeting with Guy Morgan...


00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.161
...the music mogul, but no.


00:04:10.335 --> 00:04:12.530
And using Bollywood
as a theme for the dance?


00:04:12.704 --> 00:04:16.162
That's totally un-American.
I don't care if it was my idea.


00:04:17.843 --> 00:04:20.107
Hello.
Oh. Oh.


00:04:20.279 --> 00:04:22.975
I'm Dean Van Ravensway,
and you must be...


00:04:23.148 --> 00:04:26.242
- Guy Morgan.
- Ah, yes. Guy Morgan, a pleasure.


00:04:26.418 --> 00:04:27.908
You look like a man who knows things.


00:04:28.086 --> 00:04:30.646
Aha, even some things I shouldn't know.


00:04:30.822 --> 00:04:32.619
- And I'm Luke.
Great.


00:04:46.171 --> 00:04:50.130
<i>So tell me, Guy, is it true?
Are you the new judge on Idol?</i>


00:04:50.309 --> 00:04:53.676
Well, let's just say
that Randy may be in the doghouse.


00:04:53.845 --> 00:04:55.710
- Now, let's talk about my son.
- Of course.


00:04:55.881 --> 00:04:58.315
- Have you reviewed your schedule, Luke?
- Yes, I have.


00:04:58.483 --> 00:05:02.010
In fact, um, I'd like to add a music class.
Um, the music theory...


00:05:02.187 --> 00:05:05.748
Wellesley has a great business program.
That's why we're here.


00:05:06.258 --> 00:05:11.161
There are two types of people
in the music biz: Artists and businessmen.


00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.161
- Luke is a businessman.
- Of course.


00:05:13.665 --> 00:05:17.658
Katie, get in here. Look alive.
Make yourself useful.


00:05:21.139 --> 00:05:23.471
Luke is gonna need a tour of the campus.


00:05:23.942 --> 00:05:29.005
So text Bev and ask her
to escort Mr. Morgan around campus.


00:05:29.314 --> 00:05:32.442
Now, Luke, if you are half as talented
a producer as your father...


00:05:32.618 --> 00:05:35.678
The verdict's still out.
He hasn't earned it.


00:05:37.356 --> 00:05:39.620
Heard the story of how I started
in the music business?


00:05:39.791 --> 00:05:43.227
- Yes, everybody's heard it, Dad.
- Then everybody should know how it goes.


00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.724
There I was,
working for The Rolling Stones...


00:05:47.899 --> 00:05:49.730
...when Mick himself...
- Dad.


00:05:51.003 --> 00:05:54.200
Fine. As I said,
the verdict is still out on my son.


00:05:54.373 --> 00:05:58.139
He just produced an album
with the Fruity Dangers?


00:05:58.310 --> 00:05:59.971
Do you mean Danger Fruit?


00:06:01.146 --> 00:06:02.909
That record was amazing.


00:06:03.081 --> 00:06:06.050
I forgot what they were called because
they made me absolutely no money.


00:06:07.552 --> 00:06:10.020
Thank you. Rare I meet anyone
who's heard their album.


00:06:10.188 --> 00:06:13.089
What, are you kidding?
They're a cult phenomenon.


00:06:13.258 --> 00:06:14.919
I'm sorry. Why are you talking?


00:06:16.461 --> 00:06:22.024
What I need is for Luke to learn
to spot a commercially viable star.


00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.361
Image drives the bottom line, right?


00:06:24.536 --> 00:06:27.903
I feel you. Would we have Bieber Fever
if he were an ugly troll?


00:06:28.073 --> 00:06:30.234
Actually, he is a tad hobbit-like, isn't he?


00:06:30.409 --> 00:06:32.775
I'd like Luke
to produce your Semester Showcase...


00:06:32.944 --> 00:06:36.846
...to see if he can identify sellable talent.
- I produce the Semester Showcase.


00:06:37.983 --> 00:06:40.076
I will double your Showcase budget.


00:06:40.585 --> 00:06:42.951
I will invite every talent scout I know.


00:06:43.522 --> 00:06:45.649
This could be the beginning
of a relationship...


00:06:45.824 --> 00:06:47.792
...between Wellesley
and Kensington Records.


00:06:47.959 --> 00:06:49.950
Looks like we have a new producer.


00:06:50.128 --> 00:06:53.097
Oh, and this is my daughter, Bev.


00:06:53.532 --> 00:06:56.296
Bev, this is the platinum-selling,
Grammy-winning...


00:06:56.468 --> 00:06:59.369
...and very handsome producer,
Guy Morgan.


00:06:59.538 --> 00:07:01.369
Could you give his son, Luke, a tour?


00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:04.407
Sure. Would you like
to see the Wellesley perks?


00:07:04.576 --> 00:07:07.204
Um, yes, brilliant. Sure.


00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:09.670
- Katie.
I love your accent.


00:07:09.848 --> 00:07:11.440
Katie.
Wanna come over tonight?


00:07:11.616 --> 00:07:13.982
What are you still doing here? Go.


00:07:14.152 --> 00:07:17.553
Guy and I have things we need to discuss.
Out. Now.


00:07:18.156 --> 00:07:23.560
So, Guy, you've gotta tell me,
what was that like working under Mick?


00:07:32.437 --> 00:07:34.132
Watch out.


00:07:34.606 --> 00:07:36.631
- Dangerous balls.
- Ha, ha. Thanks.


00:07:37.642 --> 00:07:41.237
- So you womanned up and did it?
Hey!


00:07:41.413 --> 00:07:43.210
- Oh, I did it.
Hey!


00:07:43.381 --> 00:07:45.747
- What happened?
Can we have our ball?


00:07:45.917 --> 00:07:47.282
I didn't give my CD to Luke.


00:07:47.452 --> 00:07:50.444
I snuck it in his dad's bag.


00:07:50.622 --> 00:07:54.581
But Guy Morgan has your demo.
That's huge. What you need is a champion.


00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:56.489
No, what I need is to graduate.


00:07:57.329 --> 00:07:59.229
You giving our ball back or what?


00:07:59.397 --> 00:08:03.026
Oh, do you want this?


00:08:07.839 --> 00:08:11.104
She shoots, she scores.
Unlike you, soccer boy.


00:08:13.445 --> 00:08:17.176
Oh, so spill it. Is Luke Morgan
as hot as everyone Tweets he is?


00:08:17.349 --> 00:08:18.714
Hotter.


00:08:18.884 --> 00:08:20.511
You should ask him to the dance.


00:08:20.685 --> 00:08:22.915
Because I'm so forward with guys.


00:08:23.088 --> 00:08:25.648
First time for everything, right?


00:08:32.798 --> 00:08:34.493
- Hi, Luke.
- Hello.


00:08:34.666 --> 00:08:35.894
You have to hear my demo.


00:08:36.368 --> 00:08:39.428
It's a retro-funk-jazz explosion.


00:08:39.604 --> 00:08:41.799
Back off. I was here first.


00:08:41.973 --> 00:08:45.431
Hold on, hold up. Please hold on.
My boy does not want your demos yet.


00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:47.874
Walk away. Move along. Bye.


00:08:48.046 --> 00:08:51.413
It was nice chatting
or whatever that was.


00:08:51.683 --> 00:08:54.015
- Yes, hi, I'm, uh...
- Luke Morgan, right?


00:08:54.186 --> 00:08:55.710
Who is producing the Showcase.


00:08:55.887 --> 00:08:58.788
I don't think I'm gonna do the Showcase,
so I need to keep a low profile...


00:08:58.957 --> 00:09:02.393
Yeah, yeah. Listen close now.
There's two kinds of people in this school.


00:09:02.561 --> 00:09:06.088
There are the wannabes
and there's gonnabes.


00:09:06.264 --> 00:09:11.429
You and I, we're gonnabes. What do we do?
We stay away from the wannabes, all right?


00:09:11.603 --> 00:09:15.164
And girls named Yolanda. There are three
of them and they are certifiably...


00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:17.433
Crazy? You attract
crazy women? Shocking.


00:09:17.609 --> 00:09:20.510
It may seem like I don't have game,
but ladies love a listener.


00:09:20.679 --> 00:09:22.806
Plus, I'm telling you,
let me help you find acts.


00:09:22.981 --> 00:09:26.007
- Ah, so you're a talent scout?
- Well, bottom line, I'm a DJ.


00:09:26.184 --> 00:09:28.379
- Oh, you're a DJ as well?
- Check this.


00:09:36.928 --> 00:09:38.190
Whoa.


00:09:38.363 --> 00:09:41.457
Okay, yes. You could be very useful.
It was nice meeting you.


00:09:41.633 --> 00:09:44.295
You got a girl for the dance?
Because I can hook you up.


00:09:44.469 --> 00:09:45.629
Uh, no. Thanks.


00:09:45.804 --> 00:09:49.205
Uh, but what do you know
about Bev Van Ravensway?


00:09:49.374 --> 00:09:51.035
- Supposed to see her tonight.
- Bev?


00:09:51.209 --> 00:09:52.233
- Yeah.
- She's hot...


00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:54.878
...but the girl
is mad, mad drama, okay?


00:09:55.046 --> 00:09:57.446
I am talking to you
and you don't even know my name.


00:09:57.616 --> 00:09:59.516
- I'm Mickey O'Malley.
- Mickey O'Malley.


00:09:59.684 --> 00:10:01.311
A rarity in the Irish community.


00:10:01.887 --> 00:10:03.980
Om.


00:10:04.789 --> 00:10:07.417
RAVl: Om.
- Om.


00:10:07.592 --> 00:10:09.685
- Om.
- Om!


00:10:09.861 --> 00:10:12.386
This is not a contest, Ms. Gail.


00:10:12.764 --> 00:10:14.391
Just concentrate on your breathing.


00:10:15.901 --> 00:10:17.061
My butt is numb.


00:10:17.402 --> 00:10:20.599
If your butt is suffering,
then you are suffering.


00:10:20.772 --> 00:10:24.230
In fact, your entire life is suffering. Why?


00:10:24.409 --> 00:10:27.503
Because you crave
that which is meaningless.


00:10:27.679 --> 00:10:29.670
Are you calling me shallow?


00:10:30.749 --> 00:10:36.585
No, I'm saying to stop your craving
and release your butt.


00:10:36.755 --> 00:10:40.316
Just release it. Release it, yeah.
Release that butt.


00:10:41.192 --> 00:10:44.252
<i>Release that butt
Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:44.429 --> 00:10:47.023
<i>Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:47.198 --> 00:10:48.495
Mrs. Van Ravensway?


00:10:48.667 --> 00:10:51.192
What part
of "if you interrupt my meditation...


00:10:51.369 --> 00:10:54.566
...I will jerk your tail in a knot"
do you not understand?


00:10:54.739 --> 00:10:57.173
You told me
to tell you when dinner was ready.


00:10:57.342 --> 00:11:00.743
Oh, thank God.
I'm craving some bourbon.


00:11:04.516 --> 00:11:05.983
Victor.


00:11:06.151 --> 00:11:11.384
- Oh. Um, dinner's ready.
- Tell me something I don't know.


00:11:35.046 --> 00:11:39.483
Do you have any idea how stressful it is
to run this academy?


00:11:39.818 --> 00:11:42.309
Yes, I spent the money at the spa.


00:11:43.355 --> 00:11:46.017
<i>Five thousand dollars a night
is not very expensive...</i>


00:11:46.191 --> 00:11:50.753
<i>... when you think about the alternative,
which is me having a nervous breakdown.</i>


00:11:54.065 --> 00:11:55.089
<i>Ow.</i>


00:11:55.266 --> 00:11:57.700
<i>What are you doing?
I'm on the phone.</i>


00:11:57.869 --> 00:11:59.461
<i>- I'm cleansing.
Heh, heh.</i>


00:11:59.671 --> 00:12:01.901
Mac and cheese.


00:12:02.807 --> 00:12:05.935
<i>I don't need your spiritual counseling.</i>


00:12:06.478 --> 00:12:08.036
<i>I'm thinking of firing you.</i>


00:12:13.551 --> 00:12:16.918
Pace yourself, Ms. Gail,
or you will not be one with everything.


00:12:17.088 --> 00:12:20.421
Honey, that's what I got you for.
Now, make me one with everything.


00:12:21.826 --> 00:12:25.023
This Showcase is giving me the vapors.


00:12:25.196 --> 00:12:27.289
How did this become my life?


00:12:27.465 --> 00:12:30.457
Did I ever tell you all about the time
I nearly got my big break?


00:12:30.635 --> 00:12:32.125
Yes.
- Good.


00:12:32.303 --> 00:12:33.736
Then you all know how it goes.


00:12:34.172 --> 00:12:36.367
<i>I ain't gonna leap, I'm gonna jump</i>


00:12:36.541 --> 00:12:38.873
<i>Find my way right out of this dump</i>


00:12:41.713 --> 00:12:44.580
- I had talent, and they made me...
A laughingstock.


00:12:46.351 --> 00:12:47.648
Now look at me.


00:12:47.819 --> 00:12:50.310
I got two ungrateful kids...


00:12:50.488 --> 00:12:53.480
...a dwarfish, hairy, elfin servant...


00:12:53.658 --> 00:12:55.649
...and a random
tablecloth-wearing Asian...


00:12:55.827 --> 00:12:58.057
- Indian.
- Who makes no sense at all, ever.


00:12:58.229 --> 00:12:59.992
Why don't you have another drink, Mom.


00:13:01.533 --> 00:13:03.728
Katie, napkin me.


00:13:03.902 --> 00:13:06.393
I have got to impress Guy Morgan...


00:13:06.805 --> 00:13:10.036
...so I can stop pretending to care
about this insufferable school...


00:13:10.208 --> 00:13:13.974
...and we can all move to Hollywood where
no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:14.145 --> 00:13:17.774
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:18.716 --> 00:13:21.116
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:21.286 --> 00:13:23.880
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:24.055 --> 00:13:26.922
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:27.092 --> 00:13:28.116
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:28.293 --> 00:13:30.853
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:31.029 --> 00:13:32.963
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:33.131 --> 00:13:36.157
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:36.334 --> 00:13:38.359
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:38.536 --> 00:13:40.504
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:40.672 --> 00:13:41.696
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:41.873 --> 00:13:45.741
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:49.311
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:49.481 --> 00:13:52.575
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:55.048
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:57.154
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:13:57.322 --> 00:13:59.552
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:13:59.724 --> 00:14:02.921
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:14:03.094 --> 00:14:07.360
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:07.532 --> 00:14:09.500
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:10.001 --> 00:14:13.528
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:16.074 --> 00:14:21.512
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:21.679 --> 00:14:24.239
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:24.415 --> 00:14:26.508
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:26.684 --> 00:14:28.413
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:28.586 --> 00:14:31.214
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:31.389 --> 00:14:34.722
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:34.893 --> 00:14:36.520
Again.


00:14:36.694 --> 00:14:38.252
Really? Okay.


00:14:38.429 --> 00:14:44.061
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:44.235 --> 00:14:45.361
Ouch.


00:14:45.537 --> 00:14:48.597
I could belch the song better.


00:14:50.208 --> 00:14:52.369
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:52.544 --> 00:14:54.011
Anything to forget I live here.


00:14:54.179 --> 00:14:57.080
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:14:57.248 --> 00:15:01.150
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:15:01.519 --> 00:15:05.182
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:09.394 --> 00:15:11.760
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:13.659
No.


00:15:13.831 --> 00:15:16.129
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:28.313 --> 00:15:31.612
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:31.783 --> 00:15:34.251
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:44.729 --> 00:15:47.823
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:52.704 --> 00:15:54.433
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:15:54.606 --> 00:15:55.698
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:15:55.873 --> 00:15:59.969
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:16:00.144 --> 00:16:01.475
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:16:01.646 --> 00:16:04.410
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:16:04.849 --> 00:16:06.146
Victor!


00:16:06.317 --> 00:16:09.548
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:09.721 --> 00:16:11.882
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:15.393 --> 00:16:17.020
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:26.938 --> 00:16:28.098
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:28.273 --> 00:16:29.672
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:29.841 --> 00:16:33.277
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:33.444 --> 00:16:35.105
Crap.


00:16:38.516 --> 00:16:40.211
This is insane.


00:16:40.385 --> 00:16:44.446
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:16:54.232 --> 00:16:56.325
You gotta be kidding me.


00:16:58.069 --> 00:16:59.696
Crap.


00:17:03.007 --> 00:17:06.602
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:06.778 --> 00:17:10.578
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:10.748 --> 00:17:12.875
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:13.051 --> 00:17:14.746
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:14.919 --> 00:17:17.479
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:17.655 --> 00:17:20.715
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:20.892 --> 00:17:23.122
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:23.294 --> 00:17:25.421
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:27.765 --> 00:17:29.232
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:35.406 --> 00:17:37.271
Victor.


00:17:41.112 --> 00:17:42.545
Katie?


00:17:43.748 --> 00:17:45.978
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:46.184 --> 00:17:49.449
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:52.384
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:53.424 --> 00:17:55.255
The truth. Um...


00:17:56.561 --> 00:17:59.894
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:18:00.064 --> 00:18:01.395
Naked.


00:18:02.433 --> 00:18:04.731
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:18:04.902 --> 00:18:06.426
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:08.873 --> 00:18:09.965
There.


00:18:10.141 --> 00:18:13.338
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:17.949 --> 00:18:19.576
I'm kidding.


00:18:20.118 --> 00:18:21.949
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:22.286 --> 00:18:23.310
No, no.


00:18:23.488 --> 00:18:26.889
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:27.058 --> 00:18:29.253
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:29.861 --> 00:18:34.525
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:35.032 --> 00:18:38.832
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:39.003 --> 00:18:41.597
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:45.476 --> 00:18:47.137
What is that?


00:18:47.712 --> 00:18:49.976
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:50.148 --> 00:18:52.116
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:53.317 --> 00:18:55.046
Hey. What...?


00:19:07.899 --> 00:19:10.390
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:10.568 --> 00:19:12.195
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:14.497
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:14.672 --> 00:19:16.936
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:17.108 --> 00:19:18.132
Do you hear this?


00:19:18.309 --> 00:19:19.970
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:20.144 --> 00:19:21.839
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:22.013 --> 00:19:24.345
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:24.515 --> 00:19:26.710
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:26.884 --> 00:19:28.749
She gave you a CD?


00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:32.287
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:33.524 --> 00:19:37.392
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:38.629 --> 00:19:42.725
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:44.702 --> 00:19:46.897
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:48.039 --> 00:19:49.597
So...


00:19:50.475 --> 00:19:52.602
...that meeting today...


00:19:52.777 --> 00:19:55.575
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:19:55.913 --> 00:19:57.972
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:19:58.149 --> 00:20:00.583
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:20:00.852 --> 00:20:02.046
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:20:03.521 --> 00:20:05.421
Is it as complicated as me...


00:20:05.590 --> 00:20:08.718
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:08.993 --> 00:20:12.724
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:17.635 --> 00:20:20.433
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:20.605 --> 00:20:23.665
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:23.841 --> 00:20:26.105
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:30.081 --> 00:20:31.742
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:33.417 --> 00:20:34.714
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:34.886 --> 00:20:37.980
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:38.155 --> 00:20:40.623
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:40.791 --> 00:20:42.952
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:43.127 --> 00:20:44.321
That's interesting.


00:20:44.495 --> 00:20:47.259
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:47.431 --> 00:20:48.659
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:48.833 --> 00:20:50.460
I only have cheese.


00:20:53.638 --> 00:20:55.606
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:20:55.773 --> 00:20:57.673
Your phone.


00:21:00.711 --> 00:21:03.578
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:21:03.748 --> 00:21:05.306
I have underestimated you.


00:21:05.883 --> 00:21:07.714
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:07.885 --> 00:21:10.979
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:11.155 --> 00:21:13.783
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:13.958 --> 00:21:18.156
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:18.329 --> 00:21:21.594
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:21.766 --> 00:21:25.202
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:25.369 --> 00:21:28.497
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:28.673 --> 00:21:33.804
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:35.079 --> 00:21:37.240
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:42.653 --> 00:21:47.283
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:47.458 --> 00:21:51.554
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:51.729 --> 00:21:55.495
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:21:55.967 --> 00:21:57.628
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:21:57.802 --> 00:21:59.963
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:22:03.207 --> 00:22:05.903
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:06.477 --> 00:22:09.935
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:10.381 --> 00:22:12.349
I like trouble.


00:22:13.884 --> 00:22:15.010
Hey, kids.


00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:19.756
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:19.924 --> 00:22:22.688
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:22.860 --> 00:22:26.694
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:26.998 --> 00:22:32.231
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:32.436 --> 00:22:34.904
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:35.172 --> 00:22:37.732
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:37.908 --> 00:22:39.876
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:40.044 --> 00:22:43.104
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:43.280 --> 00:22:46.340
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:46.517 --> 00:22:49.213
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:49.387 --> 00:22:52.686
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:52.857 --> 00:22:54.688
What if I don't want to?


00:22:55.793 --> 00:22:59.524
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:22:59.697 --> 00:23:01.756
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:23:01.932 --> 00:23:04.196
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:23:04.368 --> 00:23:07.929
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:08.105 --> 00:23:09.595
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:09.774 --> 00:23:11.241
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:12.843 --> 00:23:14.970
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:15.146 --> 00:23:18.274
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:18.683 --> 00:23:22.881
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:23.054 --> 00:23:26.888
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:27.058 --> 00:23:29.959
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:30.127 --> 00:23:32.391
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:32.563 --> 00:23:34.690
You are a star.


00:23:34.865 --> 00:23:39.063
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:39.236 --> 00:23:40.794
I'm a star.


00:23:40.971 --> 00:23:45.135
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:45.309 --> 00:23:47.709
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:47.878 --> 00:23:49.846
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:50.014 --> 00:23:51.572
Every part of him.


00:23:51.749 --> 00:23:55.276
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:23:55.453 --> 00:23:58.217
And just leave me out of this.


00:23:59.490 --> 00:24:02.050
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:24:02.226 --> 00:24:04.126
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:24:04.729 --> 00:24:06.629
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:06.797 --> 00:24:09.493
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:09.667 --> 00:24:11.726
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:11.902 --> 00:24:13.267
Are we clear?


00:24:13.704 --> 00:24:14.898
Crystal.


00:24:16.841 --> 00:24:19.833
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:20.010 --> 00:24:24.003
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:24.181 --> 00:24:26.649
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:26.817 --> 00:24:28.148
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:28.319 --> 00:24:30.446
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:30.621 --> 00:24:32.145
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:32.323 --> 00:24:35.690
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:35.860 --> 00:24:38.556
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:38.729 --> 00:24:40.993
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:41.165 --> 00:24:42.723
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:42.900 --> 00:24:45.027
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:45.202 --> 00:24:46.669
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:46.837 --> 00:24:49.670
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:49.840 --> 00:24:52.502
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:52.676 --> 00:24:54.439
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:24:54.612 --> 00:24:56.307
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:24:56.747 --> 00:24:59.443
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:24:59.617 --> 00:25:02.347
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:25:02.520 --> 00:25:03.714
We're here to impress.


00:25:03.888 --> 00:25:06.152
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:09.994 --> 00:25:12.462
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:12.630 --> 00:25:14.894
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:15.065 --> 00:25:17.260
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:17.434 --> 00:25:20.801
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:20.971 --> 00:25:23.496
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:23.674 --> 00:25:26.939
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:27.111 --> 00:25:32.413
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:32.583 --> 00:25:39.318
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:40.524 --> 00:25:42.014
That's good.


00:25:49.066 --> 00:25:52.365
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:53.204 --> 00:25:55.536
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:25:55.706 --> 00:25:57.606
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:25:58.642 --> 00:26:02.237
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:26:02.413 --> 00:26:04.608
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:26:04.782 --> 00:26:06.716
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:06.884 --> 00:26:12.117
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:12.289 --> 00:26:14.484
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:15.025 --> 00:26:16.788
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:16.961 --> 00:26:19.555
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:20.164 --> 00:26:23.463
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:23.634 --> 00:26:25.101
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:25.269 --> 00:26:27.294
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:27.471 --> 00:26:30.463
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:32.643 --> 00:26:35.077
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:38.616 --> 00:26:40.447
Okay.


00:26:41.018 --> 00:26:43.384
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:43.721 --> 00:26:45.484
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:45.656 --> 00:26:47.647
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:47.825 --> 00:26:49.656
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:49.827 --> 00:26:52.125
That I shall not cross.


00:26:52.596 --> 00:26:54.894
So sing something.


00:26:56.567 --> 00:26:58.034
Okay.


00:27:02.172 --> 00:27:04.970
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:27:05.142 --> 00:27:07.633
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:07.811 --> 00:27:09.210
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:09.680 --> 00:27:11.671
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:13.484 --> 00:27:15.952
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:16.120 --> 00:27:18.645
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:18.822 --> 00:27:20.414
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:20.925 --> 00:27:22.552
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:23.560 --> 00:27:26.495
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:26.664 --> 00:27:28.996
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:29.166 --> 00:27:30.633
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:32.036 --> 00:27:33.697
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:34.638 --> 00:27:37.471
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:37.641 --> 00:27:42.840
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:43.013 --> 00:27:44.571
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:45.683 --> 00:27:48.277
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:48.452 --> 00:27:51.012
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:51.188 --> 00:27:55.557
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:27:56.961 --> 00:27:59.623
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:27:59.797 --> 00:28:02.061
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:28:02.232 --> 00:28:04.894
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:28:05.069 --> 00:28:07.560
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:12.042 --> 00:28:14.169
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:14.345 --> 00:28:16.973
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:17.147 --> 00:28:20.480
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:20.751 --> 00:28:23.242
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:23.420 --> 00:28:25.411
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:25.589 --> 00:28:27.887
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:28.058 --> 00:28:29.753
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:30.027 --> 00:28:31.722
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:32.162 --> 00:28:35.996
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:36.467 --> 00:28:40.563
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:40.738 --> 00:28:41.762
...good acoustics.


00:28:42.172 --> 00:28:46.006
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:46.176 --> 00:28:47.768
If you gave them your song.


00:28:49.179 --> 00:28:50.840
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:51.582 --> 00:28:54.278
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:28:54.451 --> 00:28:55.782
Yeah.


00:28:57.454 --> 00:29:03.984
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:29:04.294 --> 00:29:05.591
You wrote that song today?


00:29:05.763 --> 00:29:09.221
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:09.500 --> 00:29:10.797
You really like this guy.


00:29:10.968 --> 00:29:12.663
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:12.836 --> 00:29:15.031
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:15.205 --> 00:29:18.697
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:20.511 --> 00:29:23.309
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:26.917 --> 00:29:29.750
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:31.789 --> 00:29:34.257
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:34.591 --> 00:29:38.083
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:38.262 --> 00:29:40.287
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:40.464 --> 00:29:41.488
Am not.


00:29:42.533 --> 00:29:45.525
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:45.702 --> 00:29:48.398
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:48.572 --> 00:29:51.132
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:51.308 --> 00:29:54.004
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:29:54.178 --> 00:29:56.112
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:29:56.280 --> 00:30:00.307
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:30:00.684 --> 00:30:03.778
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:06.723 --> 00:30:08.247
Okay.


00:30:08.559 --> 00:30:10.151
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:10.327 --> 00:30:11.658
That's my girl.


00:30:11.929 --> 00:30:15.922
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:16.100 --> 00:30:19.399
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:19.570 --> 00:30:21.333
What? Why?


00:30:21.505 --> 00:30:22.870
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:26.777 --> 00:30:28.335
Katie!


00:30:28.512 --> 00:30:31.948
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:32.116 --> 00:30:33.606
Go.


00:30:33.784 --> 00:30:35.513
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:35.686 --> 00:30:37.017
Angie, heads up.


00:30:38.989 --> 00:30:40.286
Katie!


00:30:45.496 --> 00:30:47.225
What's going on?


00:30:47.397 --> 00:30:48.830
Nothing.


00:30:48.999 --> 00:30:52.127
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:52.302 --> 00:30:54.600
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:30:54.771 --> 00:30:58.832
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:31:02.079 --> 00:31:06.243
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:06.416 --> 00:31:08.646
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:08.819 --> 00:31:10.252
Oh, no, no.


00:31:10.420 --> 00:31:12.911
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:13.090 --> 00:31:15.388
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:15.559 --> 00:31:18.255
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:18.428 --> 00:31:19.452
Fun.


00:31:19.630 --> 00:31:22.758
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:22.933 --> 00:31:26.334
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:27.204 --> 00:31:29.229
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:33.210 --> 00:31:35.576
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:35.913 --> 00:31:38.177
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:38.482 --> 00:31:41.576
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:41.852 --> 00:31:45.015
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:45.355 --> 00:31:48.415
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:48.592 --> 00:31:50.992
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:51.161 --> 00:31:54.096
So let's just get this party started.


00:31:54.264 --> 00:31:58.291
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:31:58.569 --> 00:32:01.868
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:32:03.073 --> 00:32:04.370
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:14.351 --> 00:32:16.615
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:16.787 --> 00:32:18.982
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:19.590 --> 00:32:22.616
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:23.794 --> 00:32:26.922
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:27.698 --> 00:32:29.962
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:30.133 --> 00:32:32.431
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:32.603 --> 00:32:35.800
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:39.009 --> 00:32:41.637
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:41.812 --> 00:32:44.872
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:45.048 --> 00:32:48.245
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:49.152 --> 00:32:52.019
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:52.189 --> 00:32:54.248
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:32:54.424 --> 00:32:55.516
I'm talking to Luke.


00:32:56.126 --> 00:32:58.617
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:32:58.795 --> 00:33:00.262
...before Gail gets here.


00:33:00.998 --> 00:33:02.329
What about the demon spawn?


00:33:02.499 --> 00:33:03.523
Mm-hm.


00:33:03.700 --> 00:33:05.099
Right.


00:33:06.103 --> 00:33:07.502
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:10.574 --> 00:33:11.836
Hmm.


00:33:16.647 --> 00:33:18.638
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:19.316 --> 00:33:20.340
Ravi?


00:33:22.019 --> 00:33:24.544
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:24.721 --> 00:33:27.155
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:29.293 --> 00:33:31.853
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:32.029 --> 00:33:33.223
Obviously.


00:33:33.764 --> 00:33:36.255
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:36.433 --> 00:33:37.991
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:38.168 --> 00:33:41.535
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:42.072 --> 00:33:45.200
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:45.375 --> 00:33:48.037
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:48.412 --> 00:33:51.813
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:51.982 --> 00:33:53.847
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:33:54.217 --> 00:33:55.741
But I never got my shot.


00:33:55.919 --> 00:33:58.149
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:33:58.322 --> 00:34:00.722
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:34:00.891 --> 00:34:03.086
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:34:03.260 --> 00:34:04.750
"Who is asking?"


00:34:05.028 --> 00:34:08.395
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:08.565 --> 00:34:11.159
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:11.335 --> 00:34:15.704
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:16.006 --> 00:34:18.270
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:18.442 --> 00:34:20.842
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:21.178 --> 00:34:23.806
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:23.980 --> 00:34:25.174
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:26.383 --> 00:34:29.079
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:31.888 --> 00:34:35.551
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:36.226 --> 00:34:38.285
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:38.462 --> 00:34:40.930
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:41.098 --> 00:34:42.156
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:43.734 --> 00:34:45.065
Blow it up.


00:34:47.003 --> 00:34:48.561
Thank you.


00:34:58.382 --> 00:34:59.781
Whoa.


00:34:59.950 --> 00:35:02.578
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:35:02.753 --> 00:35:05.813
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:07.190 --> 00:35:09.522
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:09.693 --> 00:35:12.924
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:15.632 --> 00:35:18.601
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:18.769 --> 00:35:22.398
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:23.106 --> 00:35:25.438
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:30.814 --> 00:35:32.247
Where is he?


00:35:33.083 --> 00:35:35.881
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:36.052 --> 00:35:37.713
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:37.888 --> 00:35:40.322
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:43.827 --> 00:35:47.388
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:47.564 --> 00:35:50.897
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:51.067 --> 00:35:53.262
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:53.470 --> 00:35:56.200
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:35:56.373 --> 00:35:58.807
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:36:05.615 --> 00:36:06.673
I think I found him.


00:36:06.850 --> 00:36:09.114
Well, he is blond.


00:36:12.222 --> 00:36:14.520
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:16.426 --> 00:36:18.724
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:18.895 --> 00:36:20.294
What are you doing here?


00:36:20.464 --> 00:36:23.297
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:23.467 --> 00:36:25.492
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:25.669 --> 00:36:28.604
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:28.772 --> 00:36:30.603
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:30.774 --> 00:36:33.242
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:35.679 --> 00:36:37.806
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:39.349 --> 00:36:42.785
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:42.953 --> 00:36:45.148
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:45.322 --> 00:36:48.189
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:48.358 --> 00:36:50.292
...and you're fired.


00:36:53.330 --> 00:36:56.857
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:36:59.469 --> 00:37:00.959
I heard you sing at school.


00:37:01.204 --> 00:37:02.330
You were amazing.


00:37:02.506 --> 00:37:03.564
Do I know you?


00:37:07.911 --> 00:37:10.505
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:12.849 --> 00:37:14.908
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:15.552 --> 00:37:18.043
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:22.559 --> 00:37:25.392
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:25.562 --> 00:37:26.927
Miss Van R.


00:37:27.564 --> 00:37:29.964
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:30.133 --> 00:37:31.327
...but were never good enough?


00:37:32.702 --> 00:37:34.363
Who told you that?


00:37:52.088 --> 00:37:53.521
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:53.690 --> 00:37:56.887
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:37:57.060 --> 00:37:58.186
Oh!


00:37:58.361 --> 00:38:02.593
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:06.937 --> 00:38:10.031
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:10.206 --> 00:38:13.107
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:17.881 --> 00:38:20.611
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:20.951 --> 00:38:23.647
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:23.820 --> 00:38:25.082
Follow me.


00:38:30.126 --> 00:38:31.957
Oh, wow.


00:38:34.431 --> 00:38:39.994
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:40.870 --> 00:38:42.770
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:42.939 --> 00:38:46.636
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:48.144 --> 00:38:49.338
Or not.


00:38:51.615 --> 00:38:54.641
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:39:00.857 --> 00:39:04.418
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:39:05.729 --> 00:39:09.961
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:10.133 --> 00:39:13.660
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:13.837 --> 00:39:17.830
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:19.809 --> 00:39:23.142
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:24.914 --> 00:39:28.611
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:29.285 --> 00:39:32.982
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:33.456 --> 00:39:36.289
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:36.760 --> 00:39:37.852
Uh-uh.


00:42:16.786 --> 00:42:19.380
I think I've blown something.


00:42:19.556 --> 00:42:22.616
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:25.228 --> 00:42:26.786
Move it, fatso.


00:42:28.531 --> 00:42:35.130
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:35.872 --> 00:42:39.501
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:52.055 --> 00:42:53.488
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:53.656 --> 00:42:55.681
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:42:55.859 --> 00:42:58.419
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:42:58.595 --> 00:43:00.563
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:43:03.032 --> 00:43:04.397
I'm so sorry.


00:43:05.101 --> 00:43:06.329
What...? You...?


00:43:07.036 --> 00:43:08.697
Hey. Wait.


00:43:08.872 --> 00:43:10.100
But who are you?


00:43:10.273 --> 00:43:12.867
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:21.017 --> 00:43:24.043
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:42.505 --> 00:43:44.530
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:45.308 --> 00:43:48.243
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:48.678 --> 00:43:51.613
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:51.948 --> 00:43:54.143
Don't talk about her like that.


00:43:56.152 --> 00:43:59.315
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:43:59.489 --> 00:44:03.050
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:44:03.226 --> 00:44:05.490
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:44:05.662 --> 00:44:08.722
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:09.032 --> 00:44:12.160
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:13.069 --> 00:44:16.197
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:22.712 --> 00:44:25.943
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:26.115 --> 00:44:28.174
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:28.351 --> 00:44:30.285
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:30.453 --> 00:44:32.148
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:32.322 --> 00:44:34.620
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:35.992 --> 00:44:40.122
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:41.097 --> 00:44:44.692
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:45.768 --> 00:44:47.395
We're recording.


00:44:47.704 --> 00:44:49.535
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:49.706 --> 00:44:50.934
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:51.541 --> 00:44:53.475
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:53.643 --> 00:44:55.372
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:44:55.545 --> 00:44:57.877
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:44:58.047 --> 00:44:59.275
Check this out, all right?


00:44:59.449 --> 00:45:03.044
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:45:03.219 --> 00:45:05.050
...have music during the sixth period.


00:45:05.221 --> 00:45:07.052
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:07.256 --> 00:45:09.281
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:09.459 --> 00:45:10.619
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:10.793 --> 00:45:12.761
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:12.929 --> 00:45:14.794
That was subpar at best.


00:45:14.964 --> 00:45:17.489
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:18.234 --> 00:45:21.533
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:21.704 --> 00:45:23.262
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:23.439 --> 00:45:25.805
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:25.975 --> 00:45:29.001
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:29.178 --> 00:45:32.272
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:32.448 --> 00:45:34.006
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:34.450 --> 00:45:37.317
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:37.854 --> 00:45:41.415
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:41.691 --> 00:45:45.024
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:45.194 --> 00:45:47.788
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:47.964 --> 00:45:50.432
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:50.600 --> 00:45:53.694
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:53.870 --> 00:45:56.395
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:45:58.141 --> 00:46:02.737
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:46:02.912 --> 00:46:05.881
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:06.049 --> 00:46:08.882
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:14.924 --> 00:46:18.121
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:37.246 --> 00:46:39.544
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:39.715 --> 00:46:40.909
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:41.084 --> 00:46:43.382
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:43.553 --> 00:46:44.918
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:45.755 --> 00:46:47.882
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:48.057 --> 00:46:49.183
This is not good.


00:46:50.760 --> 00:46:52.557
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:52.728 --> 00:46:54.559
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:46:54.730 --> 00:46:57.130
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:46:57.300 --> 00:47:00.736
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:47:00.903 --> 00:47:01.927
Listen...


00:47:02.105 --> 00:47:05.541
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:47:05.708 --> 00:47:07.369
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:19.222 --> 00:47:23.215
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:23.392 --> 00:47:26.384
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:26.562 --> 00:47:30.191
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:30.366 --> 00:47:34.302
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:34.470 --> 00:47:38.270
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:38.808 --> 00:47:41.709
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:41.878 --> 00:47:44.938
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:46.749 --> 00:47:48.683
It was you?


00:47:49.352 --> 00:47:52.446
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:53.389 --> 00:47:57.223
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:47:58.861 --> 00:48:01.887
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:48:02.064 --> 00:48:04.828
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:48:05.001 --> 00:48:07.128
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:07.770 --> 00:48:10.500
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:10.773 --> 00:48:12.536
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:12.708 --> 00:48:16.075
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:16.245 --> 00:48:18.509
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:20.016 --> 00:48:21.813
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:21.984 --> 00:48:23.076
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:24.020 --> 00:48:25.487
You have a date with detention.


00:48:25.655 --> 00:48:27.122
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:27.290 --> 00:48:29.019
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:29.192 --> 00:48:31.888
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:32.061 --> 00:48:35.189
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:35.364 --> 00:48:36.854
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:37.033 --> 00:48:38.933
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:39.101 --> 00:48:41.899
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:42.071 --> 00:48:44.437
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:44.607 --> 00:48:46.074
Fine.


00:48:46.876 --> 00:48:48.400
I hate you.


00:48:52.048 --> 00:48:56.178
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:48:56.452 --> 00:48:58.386
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:49:04.961 --> 00:49:06.588
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:06.762 --> 00:49:09.959
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:10.132 --> 00:49:11.599
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:11.767 --> 00:49:14.565
Chores. Bores. Sores.


00:49:14.737 --> 00:49:16.932
Katie, I've got a new task for you.


